=head1 PhoneNumberInstance

See also L<Twilio::InstanceResource>.

It has C<fetch>, which work as they do on the context.

Its fields are:

=over

=item call_forwarding

An object that contains information on the unconditional call forwarding status
of mobile phone number.

=item caller_name

An object that contains caller name information based on
L<CNAM|https://support.twilio.com/hc/en-us/articles/360051670533-Getting-Started-with-CNAM-Caller-ID>.

=item calling_country_code

International dialing prefix of the phone number defined in the E.164 standard.

=item country_code

The phone number's L<ISO country
code|https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1_alpha-2>.

=item identity_match

An object that contains identity match information. The result of comparing
user-provided information including name, address, date of birth, national ID,
against authoritative phone-based data sources

=item line_status

An object that contains line status information for a mobile phone number.

=item line_type_intelligence

An object that contains line type information including the carrier name,
mobile country code, and mobile network code.

=item national_format

The phone number in L<national
format|https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_conventions_for_writing_telephone_numbers>.

=item phone_number

The phone number in L<E.164|https://www.twilio.com/docs/glossary/what-e164>
format, which consists of a + followed by the country code and subscriber
number.

=item phone_number_quality_score

An object that contains information of a mobile phone number quality score.
Quality score will return a risk score about the phone number.

=item pre_fill

An object that contains pre fill information. pre_fill will return PII
information associated with the phone number like first name, last name,
address line, country code, state and postal code.

=item reassigned_number

An object that contains reassigned number information. Reassigned Numbers will
return a phone number's reassignment status given a phone number and date

=item sim_swap

An object that contains information on the last date the subscriber identity
module (SIM) was changed for a mobile phone number.

=item sms_pumping_risk

An object that contains information on if a phone number has been currently or
previously blocked by Verify Fraud Guard for receiving malicious SMS pumping
traffic as well as other signals associated with risky carriers and low
conversion rates.

=item url

The absolute URL of the resource.

=item valid

Boolean which indicates if the phone number is in a valid range that can be
freely assigned by a carrier to a user.

=item validation_errors

Contains reasons why a phone number is invalid. Possible values: TOO_SHORT,
TOO_LONG, INVALID_BUT_POSSIBLE, INVALID_COUNTRY_CODE, INVALID_LENGTH,
NOT_A_NUMBER.

